{{!-- ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     One written page of the Notes tab.

     This exists because the decision it makes was written out eight times, and
     every one of the eight had the same bug:

         {{#if details.bio}}   <div>…the html…</div>
         {{else if unlocked}}  <textarea …></textarea>

     Read that again. The editor appears only when the field is EMPTY. A page
     could be written once and never edited afterwards — and the textarea was
     rendered with nothing between its tags anyway, so even that first write
     started from blank no matter what was already stored.

     A page works as a journal page's text does: Foundry's own editor
     (<prose-mirror>) in its toggled form - the text shown as written, links
     live, and the pencil opens the editor on the stored markup, which its save
     writes back unchanged. For anyone who may write on the sheet, padlock or
     not; everyone else reads the text. Saving: see the detail-html listener in
     A5eCharacterSheet.

     It was a textarea handed the page as plain text, behind the padlock, and
     each edit wrapped the lines in paragraphs again: bold, italics, lists and
     links were gone the moment a page was edited.

     Takes:  label     the heading
             html      the field as stored, for the editor
             enriched  the field enriched, for reading
             path      where to write it, e.g. system.details.bio
             hint      shown in an empty page
             flat      true to leave the heading off (the four personality
                       fields sit under one shared heading)
     ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
{{#if @root.details.canWrite}}
  <prose-mirror class="am-bio-editor" toggled data-action="detail-html"
    data-path="{{path}}" aria-label="{{label}}" style='--am-hint: "{{hint}}"'
    value="{{html}}">{{{enriched}}}</prose-mirror>
{{else if html}}
  <div class="am-origin-desc">{{{enriched}}}</div>
{{/if}}
